--TEST--
the bytes of a `secret` literal are concealed, and so is an interpolation slot whose value carries `secret` — the second inside an `echo` the checker refuses, which is exactly where the value would otherwise be on screen, `rule:security/redaction-ranges-come-from-the-server`, `rule:security/redaction-covers-bytes-only`
--FILE--
<?nvs
secret string $key = "sk-live-abcdef";
echo "prefix $key suffix";
--REQUEST--
redactions
--EXPECT--
